\newlabel{fig:CNN}{{3.10}{58}{Scheme of a typical CNN formed by two convolutional layers, two pooling layers that perform subsampling and a fully connected part that provides the final output. Image sourced from Wikimedia Commons under a Creative Commons license. Source: \href {https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Typical_cnn.png}{Wikimedia}}{figure.caption.15}{}}
